 "honest_limits": [
  "Run-to-run GPU nondeterminism is NOT zero: the identical single-cohort 125-step command returned 7.120 in one process and 7.957 in another (gap_closed 0.332 vs 0.253), so differences below ~0.8 MSE at 125 steps are not effects.  The long arms differ by much more than that.",
  "The held-out arms use eval_seed 999, where the cohort builder skips 1 of 8 rows as un-embeddable, so the held-out cohort has 7 clouds, not 8.  The zero baseline differs (9.008 vs 10.652) and held-out numbers are NOT comparable to in-rotation numbers.",
  "The radial ceiling reported by wfa107h is an ORACLE bound (it uses the target to pick the coefficient), so it is not a reachable number and is not used as a denominator here.",
  "Each arm is one seed.  The 'null' readings (C=32, 100 cohorts, sinusoidal t) are nulls against a single-seed spread, not equivalence tests."
 ],
